From: ppenguin <hieronymusv@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:10:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] feat(shares): external Samba main config (include-only
 mode)

CasaOS writes and tracks /etc/samba/smb.conf itself, and refuses any
main config it did not write. On a host whose configuration management
owns smb.conf (NixOS, image-based appliances, Ansible-managed servers)
that is a conflict: the file is regenerated from elsewhere, and on NixOS
it is a symlink into the store, which the tracked reader rejects, so
every share operation failed.

[server] SambaMainConfig = external (default "managed", unchanged) makes
the main config the host's: it is never read, written, verified or
backed up, and no legacy migration runs against it. CasaOS manages only
the shares fragment (smb.casa.conf) with the existing compare-and-swap
publication, testparm validation and rollback. Reconcile and Init check,
read-only, that the main config includes the fragment and fail loudly
if it does not, instead of publishing shares that are never served.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
